# Line-ending policy for this repository. See issue #570 for the measurements.
#
# Without this file the repository states no policy at all, so the working-tree
# form of every checkout is decided by whatever `core.autocrlf` the machine
# happens to carry -- per-user config, not versioned, and different for every
# contributor.
#
# On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` that produced a standing false
# positive. `npm run validate` rewrites
# web/src/components/__snapshots__/ModelPassport.test.tsx.snap with LF endings.
# Git had recorded the CRLF checkout's size (40484 bytes) in the index stat
# cache, and the LF rewrite is 40475 bytes, so the sizes disagreed. Git treats a
# size mismatch as a modification without hashing the file, so `git status`
# reported the snapshot modified while `git diff` reported nothing whatsoever --
# the working-tree bytes hashed to the stored blob exactly.
#
# A path that reads as modified with an empty diff is indistinguishable from a
# real uncommitted change to anyone checking their own scope before handing off,
# and `git add -A` stages it just the same. The only thing that kept that from
# corrupting an unrelated commit was that this particular rewrite happened to be
# content-identical, which is a coincidence rather than a refusal by git.
#
# `eol=lf` is the half that fixes it: it pins the working-tree form to LF on
# every platform, so a checkout matches byte-for-byte what the tooling writes
# and no size ever disagrees. `text=auto` on its own would leave the working
# tree on `core.eol`, which is native -- CRLF on Windows -- and the churn would
# continue unchanged. `text=auto` is still worth stating, because it is what
# normalises newly added files to LF in the index and what keeps genuinely
# binary content out of the conversion.
#
# Deliberate limit: git does not convert a path whose indexed blob already
# contains CR, so adding this file renormalises nothing and changes no tracked
# content. 75 blobs are currently stored with CRLF and are left exactly as they
# are. Converting them is a real decision with a real diff and belongs on its
# own issue rather than arriving as a side effect of this one.
* text=auto eol=lf
